WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:01.888
- Good morning Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:01.888 --> 00:00:03.346
My one word is believe

00:00:03.346 --> 00:00:05.677
and I believe that you
have something special that

00:00:05.677 --> 00:00:09.244
when you unleash it, it will
be able to change the world.

00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:10.158
So, to help you on your journey,

00:00:10.158 --> 00:00:13.821
today's message is live
your life to the fullest.

00:00:13.821 --> 00:00:15.817
Over to you, Oprah Winfrey.

00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:17.719
(rooster crows)

00:00:17.719 --> 00:00:20.314
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:20.314 --> 00:00:22.909
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:00:22.909 --> 00:00:27.192
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:27.192 --> 00:00:29.592
- What drives you to keep working so hard?

00:00:29.592 --> 00:00:33.427
You and I are in the 60s category.

00:00:33.427 --> 00:00:34.802
And so when you're in your 60s,

00:00:34.802 --> 00:00:36.481
you know you've lived more
than you're going to live,

00:00:36.481 --> 00:00:37.598
realistically.
- Yeah.

00:00:37.598 --> 00:00:38.961
- So, when you realize you've lived

00:00:38.961 --> 00:00:40.334
more than you're going
to live you can say,

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:41.256
why not relax a little bit?

00:00:41.256 --> 00:00:42.447
Why not just ease up?

00:00:42.447 --> 00:00:43.905
Why have you decided to even work harder

00:00:43.905 --> 00:00:45.338
than you did before?

00:00:45.338 --> 00:00:47.655
- Because I think, David, that everybody

00:00:47.655 --> 00:00:50.083
you know, the thing that works for me

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.902
all these years whether it was

00:00:51.902 --> 00:00:54.798
the magazine, which I still have,

00:00:54.798 --> 00:00:57.661
or whether it was the show,

00:00:57.661 --> 00:01:00.264
I understood that there's
a common denominator

00:01:00.264 --> 00:01:01.765
in the human experience.

00:01:01.765 --> 00:01:03.782
And I want the same thing you want,

00:01:03.782 --> 00:01:05.650
which is the same thing
you want and you want.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:09.150
What we all want is to be able to live out

00:01:10.321 --> 00:01:12.798
the truest, highest expression

00:01:12.798 --> 00:01:15.570
of ourselves as a human being.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:18.210
That doesn't end until
you take your last breath.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:21.655
What is the truest, highest vision

00:01:21.655 --> 00:01:23.207
that you hold for yourself?

00:01:23.207 --> 00:01:25.205
No matter where you are in your life,

00:01:25.205 --> 00:01:26.854
there's always the next level.

00:01:26.854 --> 00:01:28.898
There's always a next
level to the last breath.

00:01:28.898 --> 00:01:31.796
So, I feel that I always knew that

00:01:31.796 --> 00:01:34.020
I would be done with the show when

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.715
I felt like, oh, I've said as much

00:01:35.715 --> 00:01:39.125
as I could say here on this platform.

00:01:39.125 --> 00:01:40.872
And then how will I be used?

00:01:40.872 --> 00:01:43.700
If there were a theme song to my life,

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.176
Amazing Grace would be one of them

00:01:45.176 --> 00:01:47.412
and Keep On Using Me to Use Me Up

00:01:47.412 --> 00:01:48.461
would be another one.

00:01:48.461 --> 00:01:50.076
(audience laughs)

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.352
You know that Bill Withers song?

00:01:51.352 --> 00:01:53.476
♫ Da, da, da, daa

00:01:53.476 --> 00:01:57.222
So, I feel that until you have used

00:01:57.222 --> 00:01:59.928
your value as a human
being, you're not done.

00:01:59.928 --> 00:02:01.532
- I don't think most people
live their life to the fullest.

00:02:01.532 --> 00:02:03.066
I don't think people are even close.

00:02:03.066 --> 00:02:04.297
I don't think most people are even

00:02:04.297 --> 00:02:06.565
anywhere close to living
their life to the fullest.

00:02:06.565 --> 00:02:09.711
I think most people are waiting
for the weekends to come,

00:02:09.711 --> 00:02:11.868
can't wait for that vacation to come.

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:14.933
If you are counting down
the days to your vacation,

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:17.105
then, in my view, I
think there's something

00:02:17.105 --> 00:02:18.471
wrong with your life.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.909
Now, there's nothing wrong with vacations,

00:02:19.909 --> 00:02:21.348
there's nothing wrong with weekends.

00:02:21.348 --> 00:02:22.998
I love spending time with my family,

00:02:22.998 --> 00:02:24.313
I love my weekends.

00:02:24.313 --> 00:02:27.478
I love vacations when
I go off to vacations.

00:02:27.478 --> 00:02:31.019
But the thing is, you want to
be running towards something.

00:02:31.019 --> 00:02:33.635
Like, a vacation or a weekend
or activities that you have

00:02:33.635 --> 00:02:35.205
should be something you run towards.

00:02:35.205 --> 00:02:38.453
But for most people a
vacation or a weekend

00:02:38.453 --> 00:02:41.087
is a running away from their current life.

00:02:41.087 --> 00:02:43.155
Your job sucks, your life sucks,

00:02:43.155 --> 00:02:44.704
and so you want to just go away,

00:02:44.704 --> 00:02:46.504
sit on the beach for two weeks

00:02:46.504 --> 00:02:48.546
and not have to worry about anything.

00:02:48.546 --> 00:02:49.755
That's not great.

00:02:49.755 --> 00:02:52.084
Like, if you get to only get off

00:02:52.084 --> 00:02:54.175
for one or two weeks a year

00:02:54.175 --> 00:02:57.143
and then you're looking
forward to the weekends

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.536
and you're spending most of your life

00:02:58.536 --> 00:02:59.886
doing work that you hate,

00:02:59.886 --> 00:03:01.194
that's not anywhere close to

00:03:01.194 --> 00:03:03.594
living your life to the fullest.

00:03:03.594 --> 00:03:04.722
Most people don't even know what

00:03:04.722 --> 00:03:07.218
living their life to
the fullest looks like.

00:03:07.218 --> 00:03:09.260
And so that's to you, if
you like dread the work

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.387
that you're doing, you're
in the wrong thing.

00:03:11.387 --> 00:03:12.992
You got to go off and do something else.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.939
That's why having
passion for your business

00:03:14.939 --> 00:03:17.406
is the most important
ingredient to success,

00:03:17.406 --> 00:03:19.424
'cause if you're only
chasing an opportunity,

00:03:19.424 --> 00:03:21.016
you'll only have some big goal,

00:03:21.016 --> 00:03:23.604
you're not going to do
the work to get there.

00:03:23.604 --> 00:03:24.883
You'll say you'll do anything,

00:03:24.883 --> 00:03:26.987
whatever it takes, right,
I'll do whatever it takes

00:03:26.987 --> 00:03:28.280
to get there but you won't.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:29.802
Because you're only motivated by the goal

00:03:29.802 --> 00:03:32.001
where you have to enjoy the daily process.

00:03:32.001 --> 00:03:33.758
You have to actually enjoy the work.

00:03:33.758 --> 00:03:35.330
And again, not everyday is amazing.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.549
Not every day is insanely successful.

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:40.181
I don't wake up everyday
and have the best day ever.

00:03:40.181 --> 00:03:42.243
There's a lot of crap
you have to deal with

00:03:42.243 --> 00:03:43.694
to be an entrepreneur.

00:03:43.694 --> 00:03:45.691
But net, like, I enjoy the work I'm doing.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.552
I enjoy making YouTube
videos for you guys.

00:03:47.552 --> 00:03:49.572
I enjoy responding to the comments.

00:03:49.572 --> 00:03:52.238
I enjoy running Toronto Dance Salsa.

00:03:52.238 --> 00:03:55.068
I enjoy helping build Lily
up to be an entrepreneur.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.362
I enjoy net, the work that I do

00:03:57.362 --> 00:04:00.022
and you need to do the
same thing in your business

00:04:00.022 --> 00:04:01.604
if you want to come anywhere close

00:04:01.604 --> 00:04:03.726
to living your life to your fullest.

00:04:03.726 --> 00:04:06.306
I agree with the Oprah in
that there is no end point.

00:04:06.306 --> 00:04:07.801
Like it's until your last breath.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:10.129
You're doing it because you love to do it.

00:04:10.129 --> 00:04:12.580
If you love doing the thing,
why do you want to stop?

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.007
If you're looking for a finish line

00:04:14.007 --> 00:04:15.234
and you can't wait to retire,

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:16.637
you're in the wrong thing.

00:04:16.637 --> 00:04:18.635
If you're counting the
days 'til your retirement

00:04:18.635 --> 00:04:19.975
or the vacation or the weekend,

00:04:19.975 --> 00:04:23.416
you are doing the wrong thing
and you need to stop ASAP

00:04:23.416 --> 00:04:25.298
to move yourself and then
you can look forward too.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.397
There is no final date.

00:04:27.397 --> 00:04:28.374
It's ongoing.

00:04:28.374 --> 00:04:29.207
It's forever.

00:04:29.207 --> 00:04:30.040
It's lifetime.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.082
It's to your last breath.

00:04:31.082 --> 00:04:32.590
That has to be the thing.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.444
And if you don't know what
that this, that's okay.

00:04:34.444 --> 00:04:35.277
Explore.

00:04:35.277 --> 00:04:36.110
Search.

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:36.996
Find it.

00:04:36.996 --> 00:04:39.056
Don't just sit on your
hands doing the same thing

00:04:39.056 --> 00:04:40.632
over and over and over and over again

00:04:40.632 --> 00:04:43.826
because the path of finding
what that things is for you

00:04:43.826 --> 00:04:45.794
that you can live your fullest life

00:04:45.794 --> 00:04:47.369
and enjoy the work that you're doing,

00:04:47.369 --> 00:04:49.279
does not come from sitting on the couch

00:04:49.279 --> 00:04:51.358
and staying in the life that you hate.

00:04:51.358 --> 00:04:52.342
That's not how you find it.

00:04:52.342 --> 00:04:54.285
You got to get out there and explore.

00:04:54.285 --> 00:04:57.781
I also applaud Oprah for
leaving the Oprah Winfrey Show

00:04:57.781 --> 00:04:59.214
at the height of her career.

00:04:59.214 --> 00:05:00.729
She had the number one talk show.

00:05:00.729 --> 00:05:02.529
She had tons of influence.

00:05:02.529 --> 00:05:04.712
Millions of people following her.

00:05:04.712 --> 00:05:06.510
And she decides to go out.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:09.841
Like she wasn't an athlete that...

00:05:09.841 --> 00:05:11.587
you're going to fade over time, right?

00:05:11.587 --> 00:05:14.386
It's not like her skills are diminishing

00:05:14.386 --> 00:05:16.279
and she's going to fall
off the cliff, right?

00:05:16.279 --> 00:05:18.858
You know, you're a 50 year
old basketball player.

00:05:18.858 --> 00:05:21.197
You can have a hard time keepin' up.

00:05:21.197 --> 00:05:22.692
She was at the height of her game

00:05:22.692 --> 00:05:23.971
and she decided to quit and move on

00:05:23.971 --> 00:05:27.332
because she felt like that part
of her life was done, right?

00:05:27.332 --> 00:05:30.408
She had said what she wanted
to say but she wasn't done,

00:05:30.408 --> 00:05:32.185
she wasn't retiring, she was moving on

00:05:32.185 --> 00:05:34.036
just to the next chapter.

00:05:34.036 --> 00:05:35.968
And so I have a lot of respect for her

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:38.375
of quitting the thing at
the height of her career

00:05:38.375 --> 00:05:40.820
to then move on and try
something brand new.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.950
And I did the same thing with my business

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:44.752
where I had my website
and that was the thing.

00:05:44.752 --> 00:05:46.658
I was all in on my website.

00:05:46.658 --> 00:05:49.081
And now I barely spend
any of time on my website.

00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:49.914
It's still there.

00:05:49.914 --> 00:05:50.798
It's still a business.

00:05:50.798 --> 00:05:52.781
I still help my team, we're growing it.

00:05:52.781 --> 00:05:54.707
But more of my effort is focused on

00:05:54.707 --> 00:05:56.321
the YouTube channel for you guys.

00:05:56.321 --> 00:05:57.316
For TDS.

00:05:57.316 --> 00:05:59.986
Lily, I'm mentoring in building her up.

00:05:59.986 --> 00:06:02.037
The other projects that I'm working on.

00:06:02.037 --> 00:06:04.514
And if I ever get sick
of the YouTube channel,

00:06:04.514 --> 00:06:05.769
if I ever have to think,

00:06:05.769 --> 00:06:09.751
"Oh god, I make YouTube vidoes, it sucks!

00:06:09.751 --> 00:06:10.584
"I hate it!"

00:06:10.584 --> 00:06:13.372
If that's ever my mindset
going into filming day,

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:14.488
I have to quit.

00:06:14.488 --> 00:06:15.479
Like I will move on.

00:06:15.479 --> 00:06:18.084
I might sell the channel
or I just might stop it.

00:06:18.084 --> 00:06:19.676
If you get to that point, right?

00:06:19.676 --> 00:06:22.032
You got to be able to
move on to something else.

00:06:22.032 --> 00:06:25.046
Now, thankfully, for me and for you guys,

00:06:25.046 --> 00:06:26.006
I love this.

00:06:26.006 --> 00:06:27.049
Like I love--

00:06:27.049 --> 00:06:27.977
I want to get better.

00:06:27.977 --> 00:06:29.114
I want to drive forward.

00:06:29.114 --> 00:06:30.466
I want to hit the next goal.

00:06:30.466 --> 00:06:32.097
I want to make these videos even better,

00:06:32.097 --> 00:06:33.989
even more impactful for you guys.

00:06:33.989 --> 00:06:37.426
But this may not continue in five years,

00:06:37.426 --> 00:06:39.428
in ten years, in 30 years.

00:06:39.428 --> 00:06:41.209
I'm still going to be
doing things that help

00:06:41.209 --> 00:06:43.286
inspire and building an entrepreneurs.

00:06:43.286 --> 00:06:44.601
It may not be through YouTube.

00:06:44.601 --> 00:06:46.134
YouTube may not even be around.

00:06:46.134 --> 00:06:47.226
And that's okay.

00:06:47.226 --> 00:06:49.134
Like the minute you
start losing your passion

00:06:49.134 --> 00:06:51.074
for whatever it is that you're doing,

00:06:51.074 --> 00:06:52.165
you need to move on.

00:06:52.165 --> 00:06:54.883
You might be able to sell the
thing that you made, right?

00:06:54.883 --> 00:06:56.071
And give it to somebody else.

00:06:56.071 --> 00:06:57.966
Or it may not be big enough to sell.

00:06:57.966 --> 00:06:58.799
That's okay.

00:06:58.799 --> 00:07:00.321
Drop it and move on to something else.

00:07:00.321 --> 00:07:02.331
As soon as you lose that passion

00:07:02.331 --> 00:07:03.730
for whatever it that you're doing,

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:06.831
you need to move on and go
find something else ASAP

00:07:06.831 --> 00:07:08.606
because the window is closing.

00:07:08.606 --> 00:07:10.943
You only have so much time on this planet.

00:07:10.943 --> 00:07:12.655
You want to do something that's meaningful

00:07:12.655 --> 00:07:15.081
and stop counting down
the days to next weekend,

00:07:15.081 --> 00:07:17.761
to next vacation, to your retirement day.

00:07:17.761 --> 00:07:19.640
So the question today is, I'm curious,

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:22.945
what is the thing that
makes you come alive most?

00:07:22.945 --> 00:07:25.848
What do you love most about
the business that you started

00:07:25.848 --> 00:07:27.984
or the business you want to start?

00:07:27.984 --> 00:07:29.588
Or something in your personal life?

00:07:29.588 --> 00:07:31.310
Like what is the thing that you wish

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.275
you could do all day long?

00:07:32.275 --> 00:07:34.138
It makes you feel the most alive.

00:07:34.138 --> 00:07:35.684
What is that thing for you?

00:07:35.684 --> 00:07:37.203
Leave it down the comments below.

00:07:37.203 --> 00:07:38.529
Really curious to find out.

00:07:38.529 --> 00:07:40.665
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to LaTrenda George.

00:07:40.665 --> 00:07:42.877
LaTrenda, thank you so much
for picking a copy of my book,

00:07:42.877 --> 00:07:43.835
Your One Word.

00:07:43.835 --> 00:07:45.421
I really really appreciate the support.

00:07:45.421 --> 00:07:46.621
And I hope you enjoy the read.

00:07:46.621 --> 00:07:47.936
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:07:47.936 --> 00:07:49.020
I believe in you.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:51.059
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:07:51.059 --> 00:07:54.023
and whatever your one word is, much love

00:07:54.023 --> 00:07:55.948
and I'll see you guys
again tomorrow morning

00:07:55.948 --> 00:07:58.490
for another shot of entspresso.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:01.268
♫ I wake up every morning

00:08:01.268 --> 00:08:04.685
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:08:07.749 --> 00:08:10.534
- Someone on another
interview was just asking me.

00:08:10.534 --> 00:08:12.544
"Hey, you know, back in the early days,

00:08:12.544 --> 00:08:14.770
"you guys released an
album almost every year.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:18.442
"You got like five albums
in six years or somethin'

00:08:18.442 --> 00:08:19.621
"and what happened?

00:08:19.621 --> 00:08:22.752
"It was eight years since
the last one honestly, dude."

00:08:22.752 --> 00:08:25.102
There's a lot more to life to do.

00:08:25.102 --> 00:08:27.512
There's a lot, you know.

00:08:27.512 --> 00:08:31.679
Vacations with families,
watching my kids grow up.

00:08:33.472 --> 00:08:35.749
Touring a lot longer than it used to be.

00:08:35.749 --> 00:08:39.168
Shit, back in those days
we had this many songs

00:08:39.168 --> 00:08:41.157
and this is how many gigs we can do

00:08:41.157 --> 00:08:43.384
and then we're back in the studio, so.

00:08:43.384 --> 00:08:46.208
A lot is happening in life and

00:08:46.208 --> 00:08:50.139
everyone in the band is on the same page

00:08:50.139 --> 00:08:52.639
which is really a great thing.

00:08:53.883 --> 00:08:55.402
We've all got kids.

00:08:55.402 --> 00:08:57.577
And we've all got other lives.

00:08:57.577 --> 00:09:00.718
But we can't live without Metallica, man.

00:09:00.718 --> 00:09:02.719
It's just somethin'
that joins us, you know.

00:09:02.719 --> 00:09:05.569
We're these friggin'
four married guys that

00:09:05.569 --> 00:09:09.180
know more about each other
than anyone knows about us,

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:10.275
maybe our wives.

00:09:10.275 --> 00:09:14.322
- If you come to the idea
of mortality once in a way,

00:09:14.322 --> 00:09:16.879
it will make you depressed.

00:09:16.879 --> 00:09:18.835
It will make you fearful.

00:09:18.835 --> 00:09:21.432
If you live with it every moment,

00:09:21.432 --> 00:09:24.879
it will make you absolutely
exuberant and alive.

00:09:24.879 --> 00:09:29.046
Because it is just this one thing.

00:09:31.986 --> 00:09:34.794
That this is not forever.

00:09:34.794 --> 00:09:37.494
This is just for a brief period of time.

00:09:37.494 --> 00:09:41.527
And the more joyful you
are, briefer it becomes.

00:09:41.527 --> 00:09:44.893
If you're ecstatic, it will
just vanish in no time.

00:09:44.893 --> 00:09:45.917
(laughs)

00:09:45.917 --> 00:09:46.750
Yes?

00:09:47.677 --> 00:09:48.907
So if you want to stretch it,

00:09:48.907 --> 00:09:51.301
you need to make yourself truly miserable.

00:09:51.301 --> 00:09:53.010
(audience laughs)

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:56.976
Otherwise, it'll be just gone in no time.

00:09:56.976 --> 00:10:01.317
If you come to terms with
this, if you live this way,

00:10:01.317 --> 00:10:05.148
that every moment, you
appreciate one thing

00:10:05.148 --> 00:10:06.502
and only one thing.

